{
  "title": "303",
  "children": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "lines": [
        "Monophonic acid bass",
        "synth built on Robin",
        "Schmidt's Open303",
        "engine, with",
        "Devilfish-inspired",
        "mods and a two-model",
        "drive stage.",
        "",
        "No sequencer of its",
        "own - drive it from",
        "any MIDI source.",
        "Pairs well with TB-3PO",
        "in another slot for",
        "generative acid."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Knobs",
      "lines": [
        "1 Cutoff",
        "  filter cutoff,",
        "  314 Hz to 2394 Hz",
        "2 Resonance",
        "3 Env Mod",
        "  envelope to cutoff",
        "4 Decay",
        "  main env decay",
        "5 Accent",
        "  accent amount",
        "6 Volume",
        "7 Drive",
        "  saturation amount.",
        "  0 bypasses it.",
        "8 Mix",
        "  drive dry/wet",
        "",
        "Waveform (Saw or",
        "Square) and Tuning",
        "are not on this page.",
        "Jog on past knob 8 to",
        "reach them.",
        "",
        "Drive and Mix also",
        "appear in the Drive",
        "submenu, next to the",
        "model switch - they",
        "are the same two",
        "values either way."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Playing It",
      "lines": [
        "Notes: note-on and",
        "note-off drive pitch",
        "and gate.",
        "",
        "Accent: any note with",
        "velocity 100 or above",
        "fires the accent",
        "envelope. Play softer",
        "than that for an",
        "unaccented note.",
        "",
        "Slide: overlap two",
        "notes - send the",
        "next note-on before",
        "the previous note-off",
        "and it slides between",
        "them. This is the",
        "same convention that",
        "TB-3PO emits, so the",
        "two work together",
        "with no setup."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "MIDI CCs",
      "lines": [
        "CC 74  Cutoff",
        "CC 71  Resonance",
        "CC 70  Env Mod",
        "CC 75  Decay",
        "CC 16  Accent",
        "CC 7   Volume",
        "CC 12  Drive",
        "CC 13  Mix",
        "CC 123 All Notes Off",
        "",
        "Waveform and Tuning",
        "have no CC. Set them",
        "from the knobs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Devilfish Mods",
      "lines": [
        "A submenu off the",
        "main page.",
        "",
        "Enable Off: stock 303",
        "behaviour, and the",
        "other knobs here do",
        "nothing at all.",
        "",
        "Enable On: extensions",
        "modelled on the real",
        "TB-303 Devilfish mod",
        "kit.",
        "",
        "Normal Decay",
        "  30 ms to 3 s",
        "  (stock is fixed at",
        "  about 1.2 s)",
        "Accent Decay",
        "  30 ms to 3 s",
        "  (stock is fixed at",
        "  200 ms)",
        "Feedback HPF",
        "  cuts bass out of",
        "  the filter's self-",
        "  feedback. Most",
        "  audible at high",
        "  resonance.",
        "Soft Attack",
        "  0.3 ms to 3 s, on",
        "  unaccented notes",
        "Slide Time",
        "  2 ms to 360 ms",
        "Shaper Drive",
        "  tanh waveshaper",
        "  before the filter"
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Drive",
      "lines": [
        "A submenu off the",
        "main page. Two",
        "models:",
        "",
        "Soft",
        "  tilt EQ, 2x over-",
        "  sampling and an",
        "  asymmetric tanh.",
        "  Warm and fairly",
        "  neutral - good for",
        "  thickening without",
        "  much colour.",
        "",
        "RAT",
        "  a ProCo RAT model",
        "  from dm-Rat: 3rd",
        "  order op-amp IIR",
        "  and an algebraic",
        "  waveshaper at 2x,",
        "  fixed mid tone",
        "  stack. Aggressive",
        "  and gritty.",
        "",
        "Drive at 0 bypasses",
        "the stage completely",
        "and costs no CPU.",
        "Mix blends it against",
        "the clean signal."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Credits",
      "lines": [
        "Open303 engine:",
        " Robin Schmidt (MIT)",
        "",
        "Devilfish params:",
        " midilab / jc303",
        " (GPL-3.0)",
        "",
        "RAT drive model:",
        " davemollen/dm-Rat",
        " (GPL-3.0)",
        "",
        "Schwung port:",
        " Charles Vestal",
        " (GPL-3.0)"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
